    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "You're listening to the voice of Nassau Community College, 90.3 WHPC. My name is Bill McIntyre and it's time for this week's Long Island news. The news show that talks to newsmakers from Nassau and Suffolk County that matter to Long Island and Long Islanders like you. So each week we'll have a conversation about issues that affect all of us. I live on Long Island just like you. I want to know more about where my tax dollars are going and I want to know more about the people making the big decisions that affect all of us. Well, today my guest to help us with this goal is Laura Gillen, who is running for Congress in New York's fourth district in the Democratic Party. The seat, currently occupied by Congresswoman Kathleen Rice. Now, if you recognize her name, it's because back in 2017, Laura was elected supervisor of the town of Hempstead. Welcome to this week's Long Island News. How are you?",
