        "text": "Inflation should be addressed by examining corporate pricing power, not just wages.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The Federal Reserve prioritizes capital interests over labor well-being.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "There is systemic bias in economic discourse toward corporate rather than worker concerns.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Lowering wages through monetary policy benefits elites but harms the middle class.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Monetary policy tools like interest rates are being misused to control workers.",
