    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "So there are these completely diametrically opposed forces at work and where the happy medium is. is always sometimes elusive to find. But we have to do something to address the cost issue. I am a mother of four kids. I go to the grocery store. I am paying education costs. So these kitchen table issues are near and dear to me. There's something that I experience every day. They're not just something to talk about on a campaign like they are for my, my opponent. There's something that I really want to do something to fix about and not just for political gamesmanship or showmanship, but because I live this existence. I pay property taxes. My opponent doesn't pay property taxes. According to legal records, he lives with his mother and father. So I'm raising four children in this community and I care about the issues that the most of the constituents in this issue care about,",
