  {
    "episode_id": 73272,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73272.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Very good, very good. And my next thing here is we want to mention some issues that you put friends center on your campaign website. You say you want to, well, here we go, fight to lower the cost of living. We just talked about that, really. So another issue you mentioned, and this is big, the salt deduction. Salt, of course, stands for state and local taxes. And under the former president, we were limited to sort of right off only $10,000, which here in New York does not cover enough. We spoke to Tom Swazie, and that was his big thing to try to get that done. He did not. What do you think? How do you approach that to get something like that?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
