        "text": "Voter turnout was relatively low in the primaries.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that motivating Democratic voters in the district could improve turnout.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Democratic voters in the district are capable of being motivated to participate in elections.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Low primary turnout indicates a potential opportunity for increased engagement.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener has some influence over Democratic voters in their district.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Motivating voters is a feasible strategy for increasing electoral participation.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker views democratic participation as valuable and worth pursuing.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 73272,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73272.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "Sure. I mean, the primary was the most unusual election I think that we've had here in recent memory in New York. I mean, we never have had a congressional primary in August. Also in like the worst week, you could possibly have an election because it's right before Labor Day, right before kids go back to school. It's known to be a week that is one of the most thought after vacation weeks. So we had and people just didn't know that there was an election because they're not used to voting for a primary election in August. So I think that explains why the turnout was so was so low. For the general election, I think we can expect to see certainly better turnout. It's an even year. There's always better turnout in even years. There's a marquee race for the governor. And I think our voters are motivated by the issues like choice and guns that are going to make them want to come out and vote this year.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
