    "turn_idx": 102,
    "turn_text": "This is probably the most important election of your lifetime. Our country could go down a really dark path to dystopian future where half the population are stripped of their rights. We see abortion on the line. And really, people like to just frame it as that. But that's women's ability to make their own medical decisions with their doctors. When their life could be on the line. As a woman who's had complicated pregnancies, there's no room for government in that decision. It is a personal healthcare decision. So we see that. That's just the tipping point. Birth control could be next. And we see My opponent also doesn't want to keep you safe. He's all about public safety. He lost his own police gun by leaving it unattended on the front seat of his car. He put a loaded gun into the hands of a criminal by doing that because it was stolen by a criminal and he wants to protect legislation that is proffered by the NRA. He doesn't want to get assault rifles off our streets. He's a risk and he doesn't tell the truth. He lies. He lies and all his entire campaign is based on a lie. First he tried to come at me about taxes. He raised taxes. I never raised taxes. I'm proud of what I did in the town of Hempstead and everything I did in the town was a good government agenda, not a partisan agenda. And that's what the voters of this district can rely on me to do, to be a voice, to speak out against the other side when they're wrong, but even to speak out against my side when I don't think they're doing the right thing. And that's what I did on that misguided law. I spoke out even though it wasn't the party line. And that's an honest representative who base is the same issues that you do, who's living the same life that you are living right now, raising a family, trying to pay for college. Those kitchen, those kitchen tables issues, grocery bills, heating costs, LMI opponent also is directly responsible for energy bills being twice as high in the town of Hempstead because he killed a bill that I put forward that would have saved residents based on published national grid rates. about 50% on their energy bills right now when they can really use that help.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
